id: unbreathable-environment
name: Unbreathable Environment
kind: battlefield
environment: true
unbreathable: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Nothing to breathe. A Survival Check on entering buys stacks of Held Breath, one
  goes every Combat Round and every Health Threshold, and running out is Suffocating.
text: >
  Unbreathable Environment. Upon entering an Unbreathable Environment, make a Survival
  Skill Check (unless you are Unnatural or otherwise unable to gain the Suffocating
  Combat Condition). For every Difficulty you exceed with this Dice Score, gain a stack
  of Held Breath. At the end of each Combat Round and each time you are knocked through
  a Health Threshold, you lose a stack of Held Breath. While you are in an Unbreathable
  Environment and have no stacks of Held Breath, you suffer from the Suffocating Combat
  Condition (this Combat Condition cannot be removed through any means except leaving
  the Unbreathable Environment, as explained below).

  Lose all stacks of Held Breath and the Suffocating Combat Condition (if it was gained
  through the rules on Unbreathable Environments) upon leaving an Unbreathable
  Environment for a Battle Environment that is not Unbreathable.

---

# No statements, and that is not this Environment doing nothing.
#
# Four things happen to a stack of Held Breath and they happen in four different places:
# the Survival Check that hands them out, the Combat Round that takes one, the Health
# Threshold that takes one, and leaving, which takes them all. A script in this language
# says "while X, Y" about the character as they stand - every one of those is an event, and
# none of them is a value.
#
# So the whole of it is in `breath.mjs`, and what this file carries is the header that says
# there is nothing to breathe here. `unbreathable: true` is the only thing anything reads.
#
# --- Where each piece lives -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   entering, leaving   registerBreathHooks in combat.mjs, watching the picker
#   the Survival Check  the Hold Breath button on the Battlefields tab
#   the Combat Round    startRound, beside the Round edge
#   the Threshold       announceThreshold, which is the one place that knows one was crossed
#   the Suffocating     settleBreath, which is the only thing that writes it
#
# --- Why the Condition is never set by hand ------------------------------------------------------
#
# "While you are in an Unbreathable Environment and have no stacks of Held Breath, you
# suffer from the Suffocating Combat Condition."
#
# While. So it is not gained once and remembered - it is true or it is not, and one function
# reads the two facts and writes it. Four callers each setting it themselves is four chances
# to set it and one to forget.
#
# --- Unnatural -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Make a Survival Skill Check (unless you are Unnatural or otherwise unable to gain the
# Suffocating Combat Condition)."
#
# Both halves of that are one question: Unnatural forbids the Condition, so anything that
# forbids it answers the same way. `unnatural` is a Slot that fans out to
# `condition.suffocating` and `condition.poisoned`, so an effect writing `forbid unnatural`
# is immune to both - and nothing here has to know which of the two reasons it was.
#
# Nothing grants it yet. It belongs to a race, and there are no races in this system.
